="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HARA TOMITARO</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATAZAWA TSUYONOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATSUTA KAZUHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARA, TOMITARO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATAZAWA, TSUYONOBU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATSUTA, KAZUHITO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HARA TOMITARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATAZAWA TSUYONOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATSUTA KAZUHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARA, TOMITARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATAZAWA, TSUYONOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATSUTA, KAZUHITO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A nonaqueous electrolyte cell having a unit cell contained in a case member of laminated film and heat-sealed along its periphery. The cell satisfies the inequality (T x R x S)/(W x C) &lt;/=0.96  mu g/Wh day where R (g/m&lt;2&gt;.day) is the water permeability when the thickness of an innermost fusion-bonded resin layer of the case member is T ( mu m), S (cm&lt;2&gt;) is the cross sectional area of the resin of a heat-sealed portion, W (cm) is the average width of the heat-sealed portion, C (Wh) is the capacitance of the unit cell. Therefore, the rate of penetration of water is 350 ( mu g/year) per unit capacitance (Wh).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une pile électrolytique non aqueuse qui possède une unité de pile renfermée dans un boîtier fait de film laminé et thermosoudé sur toute sa périphérie. La pile satisfait à l'inéquation (TxRxS)/(WxC)&lt;/=0,96  mu g/Wh par jour dans laquelle R (g/m&lt;2&gt;.jour) est la perméabilité à l'eau, l'épaisseur de la couche de résine la plus profonde collée par fusion est T  mu m, S (cm&lt;2&gt;) est la surface en coupe de la résine d'une partie thermosoudée, C (Wh) est la capacité de l'unité de pile. La vitesse de pénétration de l'eau est de 350 ( mu g/an) par capacité unitaire (Wh).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>